    {
      "type": "explain",
      "title": "Third inversion",
      "body": "A 7th chord has four notes, so it has a fourth layout: the 7th at the bottom. G7 with F lowest, F G B D, is in **third inversion**.\n\n**Why it matters:** With the 7th in the bass, the chord wants to fall a half step to the next one: G7/F to C/E is a classic smooth bass line.",
